    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d328">

                <pb facs="0425" n="415" xml:id="pg415"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.796/614: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-14T23:00:00+01:00">March 14, 1944—11
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 14—8:57 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2084. For Assistant Secretary Berle. The first sentence in my 2051 March 14, was
                    not written to dissuade you from coming here, but simply based on my assumption
                    of reasons you might have for not coming. I wanted you to come. I hear you are
                    coming. I hope you will come.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
